WEBVTT

00:01:58.698 --> 00:02:00.662
When our sexual desires are satisfied,

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:04.102
we are thrown back 
into our tormented existences,

00:02:04.102 --> 00:02:06.933
and we succeed only in maintaining
the species

00:02:06.933 --> 00:02:11.215
and perpetuating the cycle 
of human drudgery.

00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:13.504
Sounds like somebody needs a hug.

00:02:13.504 --> 00:02:16.559
Love is escape from our loneliness.

00:02:16.559 --> 00:02:20.397
According to the Nobel Prize-winning
British philosopher Bertrand Russell,

00:02:20.397 --> 00:02:24.614
we love in order to quench
our physical and psychological desires.

00:02:24.614 --> 00:02:27.180
Humans are designed to procreate,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.984
but without the ecstasy 
of passionate love,

00:02:29.984 --> 00:02:32.369
sex is unsatisfying.